From aabc3f0c2dbc9e830884a4335d4e7632c194bb24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:25:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Refuse an outside kanban_schedule/kanban_block on a
 card a live worker owns

An orchestrating chat parked t_01a1d017f26dc827 seconds after worker-2 claimed it. The park
closed the worker's open run underneath it; the worker exited rc=0 without a terminal kanban
call and the dispatcher booked a protocol violation, re-queued the card and sent a failure
notice. The creator's copy had the run and the Board's claimed event but no mirrored lease
yet, so the remote_live_lease refusal did not fire.

Option (a): a caller that does not own the run (no HERMES_KANBAN_TASK/RUN_ID for the card)
is refused with code=live_claim_park naming the claimer when the card is running under a
live local worker, an unexpired foreign Board lease, or an unexpired Board claimed event for
its open current run. Nothing changes, so the worker's run stays open and it parks its own
card when steered with kanban_comment. Unclaimed cards and a worker's own park are unchanged.

Card: t_01a1d01a0a065d6b
